  "why": "Draw This, Then Die! (Kore Kaite Shine) is a 12 episode summer 2026 run airing 2026-07-03 to 2026-09-25, so it is still on air; AniList and MyAnimeList both give episodeCount 12 and a 2026-07-03 start. anizip:19232 is the same run: it carries first-party SAME_AS handles to mal:61280 and anilist:188525, its episodeCount is 12, and its episode 1 releases 2026-07-03T14:30Z with episode 12 on 2026-09-25, the run's own first and last broadcast dates. jw:477998-503896 is the same run: it is the JustWatch season for kore-kaite-shine, it carries first-party SAME_AS handles to anilist:188525, anizip:19232, kitsu:50244, mal:61280 and offline:mal-61280, and nine of its ten episode titles repeat the AniZip titles word for word at the same numbers (Magic House, You Are Brilliant, Kokoro's Heart, Utopia, Let's All Go Together!, Comitia, The Lost World, Touch, Surfing the Cyber Seas, each with the same subtitle). Those nine pair one to one with anizip episodes 1 to 9, the two sources differing only in the glyph they put between the two halves of a title (JustWatch a tilde, AniZip a colon) and in apostrophe style; JustWatch's tenth entry is the placeholder Episode 10 and the AniZip episode 10 has no title yet, so that position is left unpaired. cr:GT00371656 holds the run: it is a bare Crunchyroll series container (scope CONTAINER, no dates, no episodes, no count) and kitsu:50244 declares PART_OF against it, with no includes range because it lists nothing to align. nf:81787975-1 is left unsettled: it is titled Draw This, Then Die and claims SAME_AS against every member, but its episodeCount is 10 against the run's 12, it carries no dates at all and its ten episodes are named Episode 1 to Episode 10, so nothing on it can be checked against the run."
